title: A2_GreekRow_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("greek_intro")>>
    Dex: Greek Row. Big lawns, white columns, and houses with more letters on them than my last report card.
    Dex: A pink sorority house on one side. A frat house that is visibly vibrating on the other.
    Roxy Vale: Welcome to Greek Week, lover boy! The Quiz Round happens right here, once you've made some friends.
    <<flag greek_intro>>
<<elseif has("sorority_pin") and has("glow_bracelet") and not flagged("act2_done")>>
    Dex: A sorority pin and a glow-stick bracelet. Roxy's going to love this.
<<endif>>
===

title: A2_Hint
---
<<if not flagged("met_tess")>>
    Dex: The sorority president on the porch looks like she's having a worse night than me. I should say hi.
<<elseif not flagged("met_chad")>>
    Dex: Tess says the frat has Fernanda. The guy guarding the frat door is the one to talk to.
<<elseif not has("toga") and not flagged("toga_on")>>
    <<if not has("bedsheet") and not flagged("took_sheet")>>
        <<if flagged("sheet_ok")>>
            Dex: Tess said I could borrow a sheet off the sorority clothesline.
        <<else>>
            Dex: I need a toga. There's a bedsheet on the sorority clothesline, but I'd better tell Tess about the toga rule first.
        <<endif>>
    <<elseif not has("safety_pin")>>
        Dex: A sheet won't stay on by itself. The DJ in the Fuse Box bar is wearing about a hundred safety pins.
    <<else>>
        Dex: Bedsheet plus safety pin equals toga. Time for some arts and crafts.
    <<endif>>
<<elseif not flagged("toga_on")>>
    Dex: I've got a toga. Chad needs to see it.
<<elseif has("fernanda")>>
    Dex: I've got a seven-foot flamingo under my arm. Tess will want her back.
<<elseif has("disco_record")>>
    Dex: Dolly's Disco Volcano record. She's going to scream. In a good way.
<<elseif has("frat_fuse")>>
    Dex: Dolly needs a thirty-amp screw-in fuse. Funny, I have exactly one of those in my pocket.
<<elseif not flagged("frat_dark")>>
    <<if not flagged("a2_met_moose")>>
        Dex: There's a big pledge standing next to Fernanda in the frat house. I should find out what his deal is.
    <<else>>
        Dex: Fernanda's in a spotlight with the whole frat watching. If the lights went out... That breaker box in the frat house looked old.
    <<endif>>
<<elseif not flagged("took_fernanda") and not flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    <<if has("pledge_beanie")>>
        Dex: I've got a pledge beanie. In the dark, I'm a pledge. Time to relieve Moose of flamingo watch.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_know_relief")>>
        Dex: Moose won't let go of Fernanda, even in the dark. I should ask him about flamingo watch. Or read the rules in the basement.
    <<elseif flagged("a2_got_beanie")>>
        Dex: I need to look like a pledge to relieve Moose.
    <<else>>
        Dex: Moose only leaves his post if another pledge relieves him. Pledges wear beanies, and the basement dryer is full of them. The blackout stopped it.
    <<endif>>
<<elseif not flagged("took_fernanda")>>
    Dex: Moose is off duty and the lights are out. Nobody is watching Fernanda. Now's my chance.
<<elseif not flagged("won_dolly")>>
    <<if not flagged("a2_know_record")>>
        Dex: Dolly has power again and wants a first request. The chalkboard in the bar says what she likes.
    <<elseif flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
        Dex: I won the record back. Dolly's waiting.
    <<elseif not has("clip_on_tie") and not flagged("a2_tie_on")>>
        <<if has("volcano_smoothie")>>
            Dex: Moose is starving, and he wears a clip-on necktie. I've got a smoothie. That's a trade.
        <<elseif flagged("a2_got_smoothie")>>
            Dex: I need a necktie to get into the sorority parlor. Moose has one.
        <<elseif not flagged("a2_know_tie_rule")>>
            Dex: Mother Whitlock has Dolly's record, inside the sorority house. I should check the sorority's front door.
        <<else>>
            Dex: The parlor needs a necktie and Moose has one, but he wants food. The Fuse Box blender works again.
        <<endif>>
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_tie_on")>>
        Dex: I've got a necktie. The sorority door is waiting for a gentleman caller.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_pr_tried")>>
        Dex: Mother Whitlock returns confiscated things to anyone who passes her parlor test. I should ask her about it.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_cb1")>>
        Dex: Mother Whitlock mocked my shirt. Tess grew up on Mother Whitlock's rules. She'll know the right answer.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_cb2")>>
        Dex: Mother Whitlock sneered at my dorm. Chad said Dunk, down in the frat basement, is the only brother who ever passed.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_cb3")>>
        Dex: The sugar question. Dolly lost the record at a tea party. She must know that one.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_cb4")>>
        Dex: The handshake and the gloves. Moose said something about his grandma being a housemother.
    <<elseif not flagged("a2_cb5")>>
        Dex: The curtains. There's an embroidered sampler on the parlor wall. Maybe it's not just decoration.
    <<else>>
        Dex: I know all five right answers. Time to take Mother Whitlock's test again.
    <<endif>>
<<elseif not flagged("won_tess")>>
    Dex: Tess is still waiting for Fernanda.
<<else>>
    Dex: A pin and a bracelet. Roxy is waiting at the podium.
<<endif>>
===

title: A2_ToCampus_Look
---
Dex: The path back to the main quad.
===
title: A2_ToCampus_Use
---
<<go campus from_map>>
===

title: A2_Bedsheet_Look
---
Dex: A plain white bedsheet drying on the sorority clothesline. Big enough for a sail. Or a toga.
===
title: A2_Bedsheet_Use
---
<<if flagged("sheet_ok")>>
    Dex: One borrowed bedsheet. It smells like lavender and organisation.
    <<give bedsheet>>
    <<flag took_sheet>>
<<else>>
    Dex: Tess is watching me over her clipboard. Stealing a sorority's laundry in front of its president is how people disappear.
    Dex: I'd better ask her first.
<<endif>>
===

title: A2_SororityDoor_Look
---
Dex: The sorority's front door: pink, with a wreath. A brass sign says "GENTLEMEN CALLERS: NECKTIES REQUIRED. NO EXCEPTIONS. NOT EVEN YOU."
<<flag a2_know_tie_rule>>
===
title: A2_SororityDoor_Use
---
<<if flagged("a2_tie_on")>>
    <<go sorority_parlor from_row>>
<<else>>
    Dex: (knock knock) The mail slot opens. Two very judgemental eyes look out.
    Mother Whitlock: Good evening. Gentlemen callers wear neckties. You appear to be wearing a fruit salad. Good night.
    Dex: The mail slot snaps shut.
    <<if flagged("toga_on")>>
        Dex: No toga, no entry over there. No necktie, no entry over here. Greek Row has a lot of dress codes.
    <<else>>
        Dex: A necktie. The only tie I own is a tie-dye shirt, and that's back in my room.
    <<endif>>
    <<flag a2_know_tie_rule>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_SororityDoor_Tie
---
Dex: I clip on Moose's necktie. Over a toga. Over a Hawaiian shirt. I am three outfits deep.
Dex: (knock knock) The mail slot opens. The eyes look at the tie for a long time.
Mother Whitlock: ...A necktie. On a bedsheet. Technically correct. The worst kind of correct. Come in.
<<take clip_on_tie>>
<<flag a2_tie_on>>
<<go sorority_parlor from_row>>
===

title: A2_Tess_Look
---
<<if flagged("won_tess")>>
    Dex: Tess Calloway, beaming at Fernanda and already planning a welcome-home brunch.
<<else>>
    Dex: Pearls, a clipboard, and the posture of someone with a five-year plan for her five-year plan.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Tess_Talk
---
<<if has("fernanda")>>
    <<jump A2_Tess_GiveFernanda>>
<<elseif not flagged("met_tess")>>
    Tess Calloway: Name? (clicks pen) You're not on my list.
    Dex: Dex Dooley. I'm not on most lists.
    Tess Calloway: Tess Calloway, chapter president. I'd love to chat, but we're in a crisis. Somebody stole Fernanda.
    Dex: Who's Fernanda?
    Tess Calloway: Our mascot! Seven feet of inflatable pink flamingo. She's stood on that stand every Greek Week since 1987.
    Tess Calloway: And by "somebody" I mean the frat across the street. Chad Thunderclap won't let a single sister through the door.
    Dex: Want me to try?
    Tess Calloway: You? (looks you up and down) ...Actually, nobody would ever suspect you of anything.
    Tess Calloway: Bring Fernanda home and you'll have the gratitude of the whole house. And mine.
    <<flag met_tess>>
<<elseif flagged("won_tess")>>
    Tess Calloway: Dex! Fernanda's home, the sisters are planning a parade, and I've scheduled it for nine fifteen.
<<elseif flagged("a2_moose_relieved") and flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Tess Calloway: The frat's dark, their guard's gone to bed... Dex, this is the moment. Go get our girl.
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Tess Calloway: Their lights just went out. Was that you? Don't answer. Plausible deniability.
<<elseif flagged("toga_on")>>
    Tess Calloway: You got inside? You're a spy now, Dex. A spy in a bedsheet.
    Tess Calloway: They'll have her on display like a trophy. You'll never get her out with everybody watching.
<<elseif has("toga")>>
    Tess Calloway: Very Roman. Now go show it to the meathead at the door.
<<elseif has("bedsheet")>>
    Tess Calloway: That sheet will slide right off you halfway up the steps. You need something to hold it together.
    Dex: Something small and pointy... I've seen someone wearing a lot of those.
<<else>>
    Tess Calloway: (checks her clipboard) Every minute Fernanda spends in that frat house, she loses a little air and a lot of dignity.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Tess_Menu
---
-> Tell her about the toga rule <<if flagged("met_chad") and not flagged("sheet_ok")>>
    Dex: Chad says it's a toga party. No toga, no entry.
    Tess Calloway: A toga party. Of course. Those cavemen think a bedsheet counts as formalwear.
    <<jump A2_Tess_SheetOk>>
-> Ask about Fernanda <<if not flagged("a2_tess_fern") and not flagged("won_tess")>>
    Tess Calloway: She has a stand, a plaque, a birthday and a fan club. The fan club is me.
    Tess Calloway: The frat has tried to steal her every year since 1987. This year they finally managed it. During my watch. On my clipboard.
    <<flag a2_tess_fern>>
    <<flag know_fernanda>>
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Ask about the sorority house <<if not flagged("a2_tess_house")>>
    Tess Calloway: Phi Lambda Alpha. Founded 1921. Thirty-one sisters, one flamingo, and Mother Whitlock.
    Dex: Mother Whitlock?
    Tess Calloway: Our housemother. She runs the parlor. Gentlemen callers wear neckties or they don't get in. Not even the pizza guy. He keeps one in his car now.
    Tess Calloway: And anything too loud, too sticky or too fun goes into her confiscation cabinet. Forever.
    <<flag a2_tess_house>>
    <<flag a2_know_tie_rule>>
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Ask how to survive Mother Whitlock's test <<if flagged("a2_pr_tried") and not flagged("a2_cb1")>>
    Tess Calloway: You took the parlor test? Brave. Did she start with your clothes? She always starts with your clothes.
    Dex: She called my shirt brave. It didn't sound like a compliment.
    Tess Calloway: Never defend the outfit. Thank her, and give the credit to someone else.
    Tess Calloway: Say "Thank you. A friend with far better taste than mine helped me choose it." She can't insult a compliment to somebody who isn't in the room.
    Dex: The other four questions?
    Tess Calloway: I only ever needed the first one. Everybody on this street has lost to her at least once. Ask around.
    <<flag a2_cb1>>
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Ask her to repeat the outfit answer <<if flagged("a2_cb1") and not flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    Tess Calloway: "Thank you. A friend with far better taste than mine helped me choose it." Chin up. Don't fidget with the toga.
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Ask about the pin <<if flagged("won_tess")>>
    Tess Calloway: It means you're a friend of the house. You can come to brunch. Nobody gets to come to brunch.
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Ask about the Quiz Round <<if flagged("won_tess")>>
    Tess Calloway: Roxy asks about the people you meet. Names, favourite things, rules. Pay attention and you'll ace it.
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Ask how she's doing
    <<if flagged("won_tess")>>
        Tess Calloway: Honestly? Best Greek Week ever. I've already colour-coded the photos.
    <<elseif flagged("toga_on")>>
        Tess Calloway: I'm fine. I'm totally fine. I've rewritten the rescue plan four times. Each one ends with you.
    <<else>>
        Tess Calloway: I've made a list of my feelings. It's laminated.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
-> Say goodbye
    <<if flagged("won_tess")>>
        Tess Calloway: Goodbye, Dex. Wear the pin where people can see it.
    <<else>>
        Tess Calloway: Go. Be sneaky. Report back.
    <<endif>>
===
title: A2_Tess_SheetOk
---
Tess Calloway: Fine. Take a sheet off our clothesline. Not the monogrammed towels. Those are for photos.
<<flag sheet_ok>>
<<jump A2_Tess_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Tess_GiveFernanda
---
Tess Calloway: FERNANDA! (throws her arms around the flamingo) She's a little deflated. So am I. We'll pump her up together.
Dex: She was the centrepiece of their party. They had a pledge guarding her around the clock.
Tess Calloway: Of course they did. She's iconic.
Tess Calloway: Dex Dooley, you are officially a friend of the house. Here, my sorority pin. It's been in my family since sophomore year.
<<take fernanda>>
<<give sorority_pin>>
<<flag won_tess>>
<<flag fernanda_home>>
Tess Calloway: And a tip for the Quiz Round: Roxy loves names. Remember Fernanda.
===
title: A2_Tess_GiveSheet
---
Tess Calloway: You're returning it already? Keep it, it's for the cause. It just needs something to hold it on you.
===
title: A2_Tess_GiveToga
---
Tess Calloway: Very Roman. Don't show me, show the meathead at the frat door.
===
title: A2_Tess_GivePin
---
Tess Calloway: Keep it on, Dex. Pins don't work in pockets.
===
title: A2_Tess_GiveTie
---
Tess Calloway: A necktie! Mother Whitlock will actually let you into the parlor. Clip it on at the front door. And stand up straight. She can smell slouching.
===
title: A2_Tess_GiveBeanie
---
Tess Calloway: Is that a frat pledge beanie? Get it away from my pearls.
===
title: A2_Tess_GiveRecord
---
Tess Calloway: Dolly's record! Out of Mother Whitlock's cabinet? Dex, that's never happened. Take it to her before Mother Whitlock changes her mind.
===

title: A2_Stand_Look
---
Dex: An empty stand with a brass plaque: "FERNANDA. Our Queen. Since 1987." Just two little flamingo footprints left.
<<flag know_fernanda>>
===
title: A2_Stand_Use
---
Dex: I give the empty stand a respectful nod. Somewhere out there, a flamingo needs me.
===
title: A2_HomeFernanda_Look
---
Dex: Fernanda, back on her stand and fully re-inflated. She looks smug. Flamingos always look smug.
===
title: A2_HomeFernanda_Use
---
Dex: I give her a high five. Her wing squeaks.
===

title: A2_Podium_Look
---
Dex: A sparkly podium with a big red buzzer. A sign says "QUIZ ROUND. Bring two keepsakes from Greek Row."
===
title: A2_Podium_Use
---
<<jump A2_Roxy_Talk>>
===

title: A2_Roxy_Look
---
<<if flagged("act2_done")>>
    Dex: Roxy Vale, touching up her lipstick in a buzzer's reflection.
<<else>>
    Dex: Roxy Vale, host of Speed Daters Live, standing next to a podium with a terrifying buzzer.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Roxy_Talk
---
<<if flagged("act2_done")>>
    Roxy Vale: You aced it, lover boy! The Dare Round is at Science Hall. It's on the campus map now.
<<elseif not flagged("a2_met_roxy")>>
    Roxy Vale: Lover boy! Welcome to Greek Week. This round is the Quiz Round.
    Roxy Vale: I ask questions about the people you've met. Get them right, you go through. Get them wrong, I buzz you. Loudly.
    Roxy Vale: But first, show me you've made friends here. Two keepsakes from two people on Greek Row.
    Dex: Friends. On Greek Row. Me. Sure.
    <<flag a2_met_roxy>>
<<elseif has("sorority_pin") and has("glow_bracelet")>>
    Roxy Vale: A pin AND a bracelet! The buzzer is warmed up, lover boy. Say the word.
<<elseif has("sorority_pin")>>
    Roxy Vale: A sorority pin! Look at you. One more keepsake and we're on.
<<elseif has("glow_bracelet")>>
    Roxy Vale: Ooh, a glow-stick bracelet. Very rave. One more keepsake and we're on.
<<else>>
    Roxy Vale: Two keepsakes from Greek Row, lover boy. Go be charming.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Roxy_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Roxy_Menu
---
-> Start the Quiz Round <<if has("sorority_pin") and has("glow_bracelet") and not flagged("act2_done")>>
    <<jump A2_QuizRound>>
-> Ask how the Quiz Round works <<if not flagged("act2_done")>>
    Roxy Vale: Five questions about the people you met tonight. Names, songs, rules. Wrong answers get a buzz and another try.
    Roxy Vale: The trick, lover boy, is listening. Most contestants only listen to themselves.
    <<jump A2_Roxy_Menu>>
-> Ask what to try next <<if not flagged("act2_done")>>
    Roxy Vale: Ooh, strategy. Tell me, lover boy, what's on your mind?
    <<jump A2_Hint>>
-> Ask about Greek Row <<if not flagged("a2_roxy_row")>>
    Roxy Vale: Tess runs the sorority. Chad runs into walls. Dolly runs the only good music on the street.
    Roxy Vale: And the sorority's housemother runs all three of them. I tried to interview her once. She corrected my posture on live TV.
    <<flag a2_roxy_row>>
    <<jump A2_Roxy_Menu>>
-> Ask about the Dare Round <<if flagged("act2_done")>>
    Roxy Vale: Science Hall. Bring courage, bring goggles, and do NOT drink anything blue.
    <<jump A2_Roxy_Menu>>
-> Ask how the show is going
    <<if flagged("act2_done")>>
        Roxy Vale: Ratings are up! The quiz clip of you is trending. Someone made it into a ringtone.
    <<elseif flagged("won_tess") or flagged("won_dolly")>>
        Roxy Vale: The producers are thrilled. Well, one is thrilled. The other one is just very caffeinated.
    <<else>>
        Roxy Vale: Great! Mostly. Our cameraman got stuck in a toga. Long story.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Roxy_Menu>>
-> Say goodbye
    Roxy Vale: Go get 'em, lover boy.
===
title: A2_Roxy_Token
---
<<if flagged("act2_done")>>
    Roxy Vale: Keep your souvenirs, lover boy. You already won this one.
<<elseif has("sorority_pin") and has("glow_bracelet")>>
    <<jump A2_QuizRound>>
<<else>>
    Roxy Vale: Cute! That's one. I need two keepsakes before we start.
<<endif>>
===

title: A2_QuizRound
---
Roxy Vale: Ladies and gentlemen, it's the Greek Week Quiz Round! Contestant Dex Dooley, are you ready?
Dex: No. Yes. Go.
Roxy Vale: Five questions about the people you met tonight. Wrong answers get a buzz and another try. Question one!
<<jump A2_Quiz1>>
===
title: A2_Quiz1
---
Roxy Vale: Lacey Rae will only dance to one singer. Who is it?
-> Hank Hollister
    Roxy Vale: Correct! Yee-haw!
    <<jump A2_Quiz2>>
-> The Grumpy Toasters
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! That's the band on your dorm wall, lover boy. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz1>>
-> Gil's snoring roommate
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! He snores, he doesn't sing. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz1>>
===
title: A2_Quiz2
---
Roxy Vale: Question two! What was the title of Ivy's poem at the Talent Round?
-> "Sonnet for the Loud Kid in the Front Row"
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! Close, but backwards. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz2>>
-> "Ode to the Quiet Kid in the Back Row"
    Roxy Vale: Correct! Somewhere in the library, Ms. Hush is quietly proud.
    <<jump A2_Quiz3>>
-> "Shhh: A Poem"
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! That's just Ms. Hush's whole personality. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz2>>
===
title: A2_Quiz3
---
Roxy Vale: Question three! What is the name of the sorority's inflatable flamingo?
-> Flora
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! Flora is a houseplant. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz3>>
-> Mrs. Pinkfeathers
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! Adorable, but no. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz3>>
-> Fernanda
    Roxy Vale: Correct!
    Tess Calloway: (from the porch) FER-NAN-DA!
    <<jump A2_Quiz4>>
===
title: A2_Quiz4
---
Roxy Vale: Question four! What must every gentleman caller wear to get into the sorority parlor?
-> A toga
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! Wrong house, lover boy. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz4>>
-> A necktie
    Roxy Vale: Correct!
    Mother Whitlock: (from an upstairs window) Correct, and stop slouching.
    <<jump A2_Quiz5>>
-> A pledge beanie
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! That gets you flamingo duty, not tea. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz4>>
===
title: A2_Quiz5
---
Roxy Vale: Final question! What is Dolly Spark's favourite song?
-> "Toga Toga Toga"
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! That's the only song the frat knows. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz5>>
-> "Disco Volcano"
    Roxy Vale: Correct!
    <<jump A2_QuizWin>>
-> "Hank Hollister Live"
    Roxy Vale: BZZZT! Wrong girl, wrong genre. Try again.
    <<jump A2_Quiz5>>
===
title: A2_QuizWin
---
Roxy Vale: Five out of five! Dex Dooley, you actually listen to people. Do you know how rare that is on television?
Tess Calloway: That's our friend of the house!
Dolly Spark: (from the bar door, airhorn) BWAAAAMP!
Moose: (from the frat lawn, half asleep) Yeah, bro!
Dex: I'd like to thank my ears. And everyone who talked to them.
Roxy Vale: You're through to round three, lover boy! The Dare Round is at Science Hall, and it's on the campus map now.
<<flag act2_done>>
<<act 3>>
Dex: Act Two, done. Science Hall is on the campus map.
===

title: A2_Chad_Look
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: Chad Thunderclap, guarding a dark frat house with total confidence.
<<else>>
    Dex: Chad Thunderclap, frat president. His neck has its own neck.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Chad_Talk
---
<<if not flagged("met_chad")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Whoa, whoa, whoa. Toga party, bro. No toga, no entry.
    Dex: I'm wearing a Hawaiian shirt. That's basically a toga with buttons.
    Chad Thunderclap: Rules are rules, bro. Togas only. And no sorority girls. They want their bird back.
    Dex: Bird? You mean Fernanda?
    Chad Thunderclap: ...I've said too much. TOGA. PARTY.
    <<flag met_chad>>
    Dex: A toga is just a bedsheet with ambition. I need a sheet, and something to keep it on me.
<<elseif flagged("won_tess")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Bro. Somebody stole our stolen flamingo. That's, like, double stealing.
    Chad Thunderclap: I'm furious. And also kind of impressed.
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Power's out, bro. The party's gone acoustic. We're just chanting now.
<<elseif flagged("toga_on")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Toga bro! Get back in there. The flamingo chant starts on the hour.
<<else>>
    Chad Thunderclap: No toga, no entry. It's not personal, bro. It's ancient Greek.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Chad_Menu
---
-> Argue that a Hawaiian shirt counts <<if not flagged("toga_on") and not flagged("a2_chad_shirt")>>
    Dex: Togas were the casual wear of their day. This shirt is the casual wear of my day. It's the same thing, historically.
    Chad Thunderclap: (thinks so hard a vein appears) ...No, bro. Draped. It has to be draped.
    <<flag a2_chad_shirt>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
-> Ask about Fernanda <<if not flagged("a2_chad_fern")>>
    <<if flagged("won_tess")>>
        Chad Thunderclap: Gone, bro. Back on her stand. She looks happier there. Don't tell anyone I said that.
    <<else>>
        Chad Thunderclap: What flamingo? ...Okay, fine. She's our guest of honour. We've been trying to borrow her since 1987.
        Chad Thunderclap: We've got our best pledge watching her around the clock. Our only pledge, actually. The other nine quit.
    <<endif>>
    <<flag a2_chad_fern>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
-> Ask about Moose <<if flagged("a2_met_moose") and not flagged("a2_chad_moose")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Moose! Best pledge ever. Follows the pledge rules like a dog follows a tennis ball.
    Chad Thunderclap: Rule two: never leave your post until another pledge relieves you. He hasn't moved since nine. I'm so proud.
    <<flag a2_chad_moose>>
    <<flag a2_know_relief>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
-> Ask about Mother Whitlock <<if flagged("a2_pr_tried") and not flagged("a2_chad_pruitt")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Bro. Don't. I've taken her parlor test eleven times.
    Chad Thunderclap: She said something about my "little frat house" and I said "YOUR little frat house!" She gave me a pamphlet on manners.
    Chad Thunderclap: Only brother who ever passed is Dunk. He lives in our basement. Like, lives lives.
    <<flag a2_chad_pruitt>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
-> Ask about the blackout <<if flagged("frat_dark") and not flagged("a2_chad_dark")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: Ancient wiring, bro. Happens every Greek Week. Somebody always plugs in one disco ball too many.
    Chad Thunderclap: The good news is the dryer finally stopped. That thing's been running since my freshman year.
    <<flag a2_chad_dark>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
-> Ask how the party's going
    <<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
        Chad Thunderclap: In the dark? Bro, it's honestly better. Nobody can see me dance.
    <<else>>
        Chad Thunderclap: Legendary, bro. We've done the toga chant, the flamingo chant, and the chant about the chants.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Menu>>
-> Say goodbye
    Chad Thunderclap: Later, bro. Toga responsibly.
===
title: A2_Chad_GiveToga
---
<<if flagged("toga_on")>>
    Chad Thunderclap: You're already wearing it, bro.
<<else>>
    Chad Thunderclap: (inspects the toga) Draped. Pinned. Tasteful. Bro... it's beautiful.
    Dex: (pulls it on over the Hawaiian shirt) Hail me.
    Chad Thunderclap: HAIL YOU, BRO! Get in there!
    <<take toga>>
    <<flag toga_on>>
    <<go frat_house from_row>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Chad_GiveSheet
---
Chad Thunderclap: Bro, that's a sheet. A toga is a sheet with commitment. Pin it or it's just bedding.
===
title: A2_Chad_GiveFernanda
---
Chad Thunderclap: Bro, you can't just hand me... wait. Is that... It's dark. I saw nothing.
===
title: A2_Chad_GiveBeanie
---
Chad Thunderclap: A pledge beanie? Bro, you don't want to be a pledge. Pledges do chores. Like breathing on command.
===
title: A2_Chad_GiveTie
---
Chad Thunderclap: A necktie? With a toga? Bro. That's two dress codes. Pick a lane.
===
title: A2_Chad_GiveSmoothie
---
Chad Thunderclap: Bro, I'm on a strict diet of root beer and confidence. Give it to somebody who's actually hungry.
===

title: A2_FratDoor_Look
---
Dex: The frat house door. It's thumping like a heartbeat. A very loud, very sweaty heartbeat.
===
title: A2_FratDoor_Use
---
<<if flagged("toga_on")>>
    <<go frat_house from_row>>
<<else>>
    <<jump A2_Chad_Talk>>
<<endif>>
===

title: A2_BarDoor_Look
---
Dex: A little bar called the Fuse Box. The neon sign is out. Fitting.
===
title: A2_BarDoor_Use
---
<<go fuse_box from_row>>
===

title: A2_Combine_Toga
---
Dex: Fold, wrap, drape, pin. I am a Roman senator. I am a bedsheet burrito. I am ready.
<<take bedsheet>>
<<take safety_pin>>
<<give toga>>
<<flag made_toga>>
===

title: A2_Frat_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("frat_intro")>>
    Dex: Thirty guys in bedsheets, a disco ball, and a keg. And there, under a spotlight...
    Dex: Fernanda! Seven feet of pink, surrounded by a whole dance floor chanting her name.
    Dex: And right next to her, a huge guy in a beanie, standing guard like a bouncer for birds.
    Dex: I can't just walk off with her. Everybody's staring right at her.
    <<flag frat_intro>>
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark") and not flagged("frat_dark_intro")>>
    Dex: Still pitch dark in here. The party has evolved into a sing-along.
    <<flag frat_dark_intro>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_FratExit_Look
---
Dex: The front door, back out to Greek Row.
===
title: A2_FratExit_Use
---
<<if has("fernanda") and not flagged("fernanda_escape")>>
    Dex: Chad's at the door. I'll just stroll past with a seven-foot flamingo. In the dark, she's just a tall friend.
    Chad Thunderclap: Night, bro. Night, tall lady.
    <<flag fernanda_escape>>
<<endif>>
<<go greek_row from_frat>>
===
title: A2_Keg_Look
---
Dex: A keg labelled "THE HARD STUFF". It's root beer. Chad's secret is safe with me.
===
title: A2_Keg_Use
---
Dex: A cup of root beer, served with confidence. Very refreshing. Very hard.
<<if flagged("a2_moose_hungry") and not flagged("a2_got_tie")>>
    Dex: Moose would kill for this. Except pledge rule three says no root beer until initiation. It has to be actual food.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Photos_Look
---
Dex: Frat photos going back to 1912. Every year, at least one guy named Chad. They might all be the same Chad.
===
title: A2_Photos_Use
---
Dex: 1987: "The Year We Almost Got the Flamingo." Looks like they've been trying for a while.
Dex: 2019: a guy in sunglasses holding a teacup, labelled "DUNK. THE ONLY ONE WHO PASSED." Passed what?
===
title: A2_Fernanda_Look
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark") and flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    Dex: A tall pink shape in the dark. Seven feet of fabulous, and nobody's watching her.
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: A tall pink shape in the dark, with a large pledge-shaped shape wrapped around it.
<<else>>
    Dex: Fernanda, under a spotlight, with a ring of guys in togas dancing around her like she's a campfire.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Fernanda_Use
---
<<if not flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: In the spotlight, with thirty guys watching and a pledge built like a vending machine standing guard? I'd be toga-tackled before I took a step.
    Dex: If only the lights went out for a minute.
<<elseif not flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    Dex: I reach for Fernanda in the dark and grab... an arm. A big arm.
    Moose: Nobody touches the bird! I've got her! I'll ALWAYS have her!
    <<if flagged("a2_know_relief")>>
        Dex: Lights out wasn't enough. Moose won't leave his post unless another pledge relieves him.
    <<else>>
        Dex: Lights out wasn't enough. I need Moose out of the way. Maybe I should ask him about this flamingo watch of his.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Dex: I tuck Fernanda under my arm. She squeaks. Somebody in the dark says "Dude, was that you?"
    Dex: Somebody else says "Is this the bathroom?" Nobody notices a flamingo leaving.
    <<give fernanda>>
    <<flag took_fernanda>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_DanceFloor_Look
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: Thirty guys bumping into each other in the dark. Somebody just apologised to a lamp.
<<else>>
    Dex: A disco ball, flashing lights, and thirty guys doing the sprinkler in bedsheets.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_DanceFloor_Use
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: I join the sing-along. It's "Toga Toga Toga". It's the only song they know.
<<else>>
    Dex: I do one sprinkler. Respectfully. A guy named Chad gives me a high five.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Breaker_Look
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: The breaker box, with an empty socket where the main fuse used to be.
<<else>>
    Dex: An ancient breaker box with old screw-in fuses, like in my grandma's basement. The big one says "MAIN 30A". It runs the whole house.
    <<if flagged("met_dolly") and not flagged("dolly_fused")>>
        Dex: Thirty amps. Old screw-in kind. That's exactly what Dolly needs.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Breaker_Use
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: Nothing left to unscrew. Unless I want to unscrew the box itself. I don't.
<<else>>
    Dex: Lefty loosey... The music dies. The lights die. Thirty guys scream at the same pitch.
    Dex: Somewhere under the floor, something big and rattly grinds to a stop.
    Dex: One thirty-amp fuse, warm and slightly sticky, now in my pocket.
    <<give frat_fuse>>
    <<flag frat_dark>>
    <<flag frat_dark_intro>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Breaker_PutBack
---
Dex: Put it back? Somebody else needs this more than a dark room full of guys in sheets.
===
title: A2_BasementDoor_Look
---
Dex: A door with a hand-painted sign: "BASEMENT. PLEDGES AND DUNK ONLY." There's a rumbling noise behind it.
===
title: A2_BasementDoor_Use
---
<<go frat_basement from_frat>>
===

title: A2_Moose_Look
---
<<if flagged("a2_got_tie")>>
    Dex: Moose: a huge pledge in a toga and a blue beanie, happily licking smoothie off his own face. He's still guarding her.
<<else>>
    Dex: A huge pledge in a toga, a blue beanie and a clip-on necktie. His stomach is growling loud enough to dance to.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_SleepMoose_Look
---
Dex: Moose, asleep on a cot, hugging a pink pillow. He misses her already.
===
title: A2_Moose_Talk
---
<<if flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    Moose: (half asleep) Zzz... I'm up. I'm up. Is it flamingo time? Is it food time?
<<elseif not flagged("a2_met_moose")>>
    Moose: HALT! (salutes) Pledge Moose, flamingo watch. Nobody touches the bird.
    Dex: I'm Dex. I wasn't going to touch her. I was going to admire her.
    Moose: Admire from behind the velvet rope, bro. Chad's orders.
    <<flag a2_met_moose>>
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Moose: (hugging Fernanda in the dark) Who's there? I've got the bird. I've ALWAYS got the bird.
<<else>>
    Moose: Still on flamingo watch, bro. Hour six. My legs went to sleep in hour four.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Moose_Menu
---
-> Ask about flamingo watch <<if not flagged("a2_moose_watch") and not flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    Moose: Pledge rule two: never leave your post until another pledge relieves you.
    Dex: So get another pledge to relieve you.
    Moose: There were ten of us. Nine quit at the toga fitting. I'm the last pledge, bro. I'm gonna be on flamingo watch till graduation.
    Moose: You'd know a pledge if you saw one. We all wear the beanie. Even in the shower.
    <<flag a2_moose_watch>>
    <<flag a2_know_relief>>
    <<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
-> Ask about his necktie <<if not flagged("a2_moose_hungry") and not flagged("a2_got_tie")>>
    Moose: Pledge rule four: wear a tie at all times. Yes, with the toga. It's a clip-on. My mom clipped it.
    Moose: I'd trade it for literally anything to eat, bro. Pledges eat last, and the brothers haven't eaten yet. They're chanting instead.
    Dex: There's root beer.
    Moose: Rule three. No root beer until initiation. Food, bro. I need food.
    <<flag a2_moose_hungry>>
    <<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
-> Ask what he'd eat <<if flagged("a2_moose_hungry") and not flagged("a2_got_tie")>>
    Moose: Anything. A sandwich. A smoothie. A crouton. I'd eat a crouton off the floor. I've considered it.
    <<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
-> Ask if he knows Mother Whitlock <<if flagged("a2_pr_tried") and not flagged("a2_cb4")>>
    Moose: The sorority housemother? Bro, my grandma Bev was a housemother for thirty years. I know the rules.
    Moose: When a housemother won't shake your hand, you bow. Grandma always said:
    Moose: "Then allow me to bow instead. It's kinder to your gloves and better for my posture."
    Moose: I practise on Fernanda. She's never once complained.
    <<flag a2_cb4>>
    <<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
-> Ask about the frat <<if not flagged("a2_moose_frat")>>
    Moose: I wanna be a brother so bad, bro. Brothers get a laurel wreath. Brothers get to sit DOWN.
    <<flag a2_moose_frat>>
    <<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
-> Ask how he's holding up
    <<if flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
        Moose: Best nap of my life, bro. I dreamed I was a flamingo. Standing on one leg was so restful.
    <<elseif flagged("a2_got_tie")>>
        Moose: Full belly. Bare neck. Living the dream, bro.
    <<else>>
        Moose: My stomach is louder than the party. Somebody tried to dance to it.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Moose_Menu>>
-> Say goodbye
    Moose: Later, bro. I'll be right here. Forever, probably.
===
title: A2_Moose_GiveSmoothie
---
<<if flagged("a2_got_tie")>>
    Moose: I already ate, bro. I'm so full I can see sounds.
<<else>>
    Moose: Is that... food? Liquid food? Orange liquid food?
    Dex: Volcano Smoothie. Mango, chilli, and something the bartender called "courage".
    Moose: (drinks it in one go) ...Bro. BRO. I can feel my legs again.
    Moose: Take the tie. Take it! Pledge rule four says wear a tie, but pledge rule zero says don't starve.
    <<take volcano_smoothie>>
    <<give clip_on_tie>>
    <<flag a2_got_tie>>
    Dex: One clip-on necktie, still warm. It has a tiny moose on it.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Moose_GiveBeanie
---
<<if flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    Moose: (snoring) Shift change... complete... Zzz.
<<elseif not flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: With the lights on he'd see it's just me in a hat. I need him not to see my face.
<<else>>
    Dex: (pulls the beanie on, and lowers my voice) Pledge reporting for flamingo watch! Shift change!
    Moose: (pats my head in the dark) Beanie... beanie... it's a pledge! Bro! A NEW PLEDGE! I'm RELIEVED!
    Moose: She likes to be told she's pretty every ten minutes. I'm going to go lie down in the basement for nine hours.
    <<take pledge_beanie>>
    <<flag a2_moose_relieved>>
    Dex: He's gone. It's just me, Fernanda, and thirty guys in the dark singing about togas.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Moose_GiveJunk
---
Moose: Can I eat it? ...No? Then no thanks, bro.
===
title: A2_Moose_GiveFuse
---
Moose: Is that a battery? Is it a snack battery? Bro, I'm so hungry I'd try.
===
title: A2_Moose_GiveFernanda
---
Moose: The bird! You have the bird! ...Wait, I'm off duty. Not my problem. Night, bro.
===

title: A2_Basement_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("a2_basement_intro")>>
    Dex: The frat basement. Concrete, a ping-pong table, a dryer that sounds like a helicopter landing, and a guy who looks like he came with the building.
    Dunk: Welcome to the Pit. Wipe your feet. Or don't. It's the Pit.
    <<flag a2_basement_intro>>
    <<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
        <<flag a2_basement_dark>>
    <<endif>>
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark") and not flagged("a2_basement_dark")>>
    Dex: It's dark down here too, apart from Dunk's lava lamp, which runs on batteries and spite.
    Dex: And it's quiet. The dryer has finally stopped.
    <<flag a2_basement_dark>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_BasementExit_Look
---
Dex: The stairs back up to the party.
===
title: A2_BasementExit_Use
---
<<go frat_house from_basement>>
===
title: A2_Dryer_Look
---
<<if flagged("a2_got_beanie")>>
    Dex: The dryer, door hanging open. Beanies. So many beanies. I only needed one.
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: The dryer's dead quiet now. The door's unlocked and hanging open. Inside: a tangle of blue pledge beanies.
<<else>>
    Dex: A dryer rattling like it's full of gravel. A red light says "DOOR LOCKED: CYCLE IN PROGRESS". The timer says "FOREVER".
    Dex: Through the little window, blue pledge beanies tumble past. Nine of them. One for each pledge who quit.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Dryer_Use
---
<<if flagged("a2_got_beanie")>>
    Dex: One beanie's plenty. Two beanies is a cry for help.
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: I fish out one blue beanie. Still warm. It says PLEDGE across the front, in case anyone forgets.
    <<give pledge_beanie>>
    <<flag a2_got_beanie>>
<<else>>
    Dex: Locked mid-cycle. I pull on the handle. The dryer pulls back. It's winning.
    <<if flagged("a2_know_dryer")>>
        Dex: Dunk said only a blackout would stop it.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_PledgeRules_Look
---
Dex: A whiteboard: "PLEDGE RULES. 1. Wear the beanie. 2. Never leave your post until another pledge relieves you. 3. No root beer until initiation. 4. Wear a tie at all times (yes, with the toga)."
Dex: Underneath, in angry capitals: "RULE 2 IS THE IMPORTANT ONE, MOOSE."
<<flag a2_know_relief>>
===
title: A2_PledgeRules_Use
---
Dex: Somebody has added "Rule 5: be cool" in a different marker. Then, in a third marker: "Rule 6: Dunk is not a pledge. Stop asking him to do chores."
===
title: A2_MascotShelf_Look
---
Dex: The frat's trophy shelf of stolen mascots: a garden gnome in a graduation cap, a plaster goat, and a foam finger the size of a canoe.
Dex: There's an empty spot at the end with a tag: "RESERVED: FLAMINGO".
===
title: A2_MascotShelf_Use
---
Dex: I pat the gnome on the head. He looks like he's seen things. Probably the goat.
===
title: A2_PingPong_Look
---
Dex: A ping-pong table with a net made of knotted socks. The scoreboard says "DUNK 4,011. EVERYONE ELSE 3".
===
title: A2_PingPong_Use
---
<<if flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dex: Ping-pong in the dark is mostly catching the ball with your face.
<<else>>
    Dex: I serve. The ball bounces off the table, the ceiling, Dunk, and into the dryer's lint trap. Game, set, lint.
<<endif>>
===

title: A2_Dunk_Look
---
Dex: A man in a faded toga from an earlier decade, sunglasses at night, and a mug that says "WORLD'S OLDEST UNDERGRAD".
===
title: A2_Dunk_Talk
---
<<if not flagged("a2_met_dunk")>>
    Dunk: Duncan Pellingham. Call me Dunk. Seventh-year senior.
    Dex: Seventh year?
    Dunk: I'm not behind, I'm thorough. I live down here now. Technically I'm a load-bearing alumnus.
    <<flag a2_met_dunk>>
<<elseif flagged("a2_moose_relieved")>>
    Dunk: (nods at the snoring cot) Look at him. First nap in three days. You did a kind thing, man.
<<elseif flagged("frat_dark")>>
    Dunk: Blackout. Classic. The '22 blackout lasted a whole weekend. We ate the ping-pong balls. Don't ask.
<<else>>
    Dunk: Dex. Pull up a beanbag. That one's mine, that one's also mine. Stand, then.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Dunk_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Dunk_Menu
---
-> Ask about the dryer <<if not flagged("a2_know_dryer")>>
    Dunk: That dryer's been running since 2021. The door locks mid-cycle and the timer's stuck on "forever".
    Dunk: It's full of pledge beanies. Every pledge who quits throws his beanie in there. It's a tradition. A loud one.
    Dunk: Only thing that'd ever stop it is a blackout. Don't tell Chad I said that. He thinks it's haunted.
    <<flag a2_know_dryer>>
    <<jump A2_Dunk_Menu>>
-> Ask about Mother Whitlock <<if not flagged("a2_cb2")>>
    Dunk: (takes off his sunglasses, slowly) The parlor test. 2019. I'm the only brother who ever passed it.
    Dunk: She tests five courtesies. Every line is a trap. Mine was the one about where I live.
    Dunk: When she sneers at your home, you never defend it. You praise hers. You say:
    Dunk: "Then I'm all the luckier to be a guest in a house as lovely as this one."
    Dunk: The other four I got from people who'd failed. Everybody on Greek Row has lost to her at least once. Ask around.
    <<flag a2_cb2>>
    <<jump A2_Dunk_Menu>>
-> Ask about the trophy shelf <<if not flagged("a2_dunk_shelf")>>
    Dunk: The gnome is from the agriculture school. The goat is from a petting zoo. The foam finger is from a stadium, and it wants to go home.
    Dunk: Fernanda was supposed to be the crown jewel. Honestly? She looks better on her own stand.
    <<flag a2_dunk_shelf>>
    <<jump A2_Dunk_Menu>>
-> Ask about Moose <<if flagged("a2_met_moose") and not flagged("a2_dunk_moose")>>
    Dunk: Good kid. Takes rules more seriously than the people who wrote them. He hasn't eaten since rush, man.
    <<flag a2_dunk_moose>>
    <<jump A2_Dunk_Menu>>
-> Ask why he's still here
    <<if flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
        Dunk: You passed the parlor test? Man. Now there's two of us. We should start a club. A quiet, polite club.
    <<else>>
        Dunk: The rent's cheap, the ping-pong is undefeated, and every year a new pledge needs someone to tell him it'll be okay.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Dunk_Menu>>
-> Say goodbye
    Dunk: Stay thorough, man.
===
title: A2_Dunk_GiveSmoothie
---
Dunk: Generous, but I'm on a strict diet of nostalgia. Give it to Moose. That kid hasn't eaten since rush.
===
title: A2_Dunk_GiveBeanie
---
Dunk: Put that on a pledge, man, not on me. I've done my time in the beanie.
===
title: A2_Dunk_GiveFernanda
---
Dunk: Fernanda! The one that got away. Well, now she's getting away again. Go, run. I didn't see a thing.
===
title: A2_Dunk_GiveTie
---
Dunk: A clip-on. I wore one exactly like it to the parlor in 2019. Stand up straight in it.
===

title: A2_Parlor_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("a2_parlor_intro")>>
    Dex: The sorority parlor. Pink wallpaper, doilies on the doilies, and a silence so polite it makes my ears sit up straight.
    Mother Whitlock: Mister Dooley. I am Mother Whitlock, housemother of Phi Lambda Alpha since before your parents met.
    Mother Whitlock: You are wearing a necktie on a bedsheet on a fruit salad. We shall discuss it. Or rather, I shall.
    <<flag a2_parlor_intro>>
    <<flag a2_met_pruitt>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_ParlorExit_Look
---
Dex: The front door, back out to the porch. Freedom smells like lawn.
===
title: A2_ParlorExit_Use
---
<<go greek_row from_parlor>>
===
title: A2_Portrait_Look
---
Dex: "PRUDENCE LAMBERT, FOUNDER, 1921." She has Mother Whitlock's eyebrows. Maybe the eyebrows get passed down, like the pin.
===
title: A2_Portrait_Use
---
Dex: I straighten the frame by one millimetre. Somewhere behind me, Mother Whitlock feels it and approves.
===
title: A2_TeaCart_Look
---
Dex: A silver tea cart. Finger sandwiches cut into perfect triangles. The crusts have been removed and, I assume, punished.
===
title: A2_TeaCart_Use
---
Mother Whitlock: Those sandwiches are counted, Mister Dooley. Twice. Once by me and once by God.
Dex: Moose would love one of these. Mother Whitlock would love catching me even more.
===
title: A2_Sampler_Look
---
Dex: An embroidered sampler in a gold frame: "RULES OF THE PARLOR, 1921."
Dex: "When lost for words, a guest should be lost for words about the drapes. Say: Forgive me, I was speechless. Are they original to the house?"
Dex: In smaller stitches: "They are."
<<flag a2_cb5>>
===
title: A2_Sampler_Use
---
Dex: Somebody stitched a tiny flamingo in the corner. Fernanda has been here a long time.
<<flag a2_cb5>>
===
title: A2_Cabinet_Look
---
Dex: A glass cabinet with a brass plate: "CONFISCATED." Inside: an airhorn, a frat water-balloon catapult, a "Toga Toga Toga" cassette, and forty-one red cups.
Dex: Each one has a little tag, with a date and a crime.
===
title: A2_Cabinet_Use
---
Dex: Locked. The key hangs on a chain around Mother Whitlock's neck, next to her other key, which is also on a chain.
===
title: A2_Record_Look
---
Dex: A vinyl record on a little display stand on top of the cabinet: "DISCO VOLCANO". The tag says "Excessive bass. Founders' Tea. The teacups have not recovered."
===
title: A2_Record_Use
---
Mother Whitlock: Hands, Mister Dooley. Confiscated property is returned only to a guest who passes the parlor test.
===

title: A2_Whitlock_Look
---
<<if flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    Dex: Mother Whitlock. She's almost smiling at me. It's terrifying in a whole new way.
<<else>>
    Dex: Mother Whitlock: lilac cardigan, white gloves, silver bun, and a teacup she holds like a weapon.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Whitlock_Talk
---
<<if flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    Mother Whitlock: Mister Dooley. You may sit. Not there. That chair is reserved for 1954.
<<elseif flagged("a2_pr_tried")>>
    Mother Whitlock: Back again. Persistence is a virtue, Mister Dooley. So is preparation.
<<else>>
    Mother Whitlock: Stand up straight, Mister Dooley. You're slouching in two directions at once.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Whitlock_Menu
---
-> Ask about Dolly's record <<if flagged("a2_know_record") and not flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    Mother Whitlock: Miss Spark. One semester a sister. She played that record at our Founders' Tea. With an airhorn.
    Mother Whitlock: The teacups vibrated off the saucers. A great-aunt fainted. Twice. Confiscated.
    Dex: Is there any way she could get it back?
    Mother Whitlock: Confiscated property is returned only to a gentleman who passes the parlor test.
    <<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
-> Ask about the parlor test <<if not flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    Mother Whitlock: Five courtesies, Mister Dooley. I say something. You answer as a gentleman would.
    Mother Whitlock: Answer all five correctly and you may reclaim one item from my confiscation cabinet.
    Mother Whitlock: Slip once and you fail. I shall finish the test anyway. It builds character. Mostly mine.
    <<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
-> Take the parlor test <<if not flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    <<jump A2_Duel_Start>>
-> Ask about the cabinet <<if not flagged("a2_pr_cab")>>
    Mother Whitlock: Fifty years of confiscations. The airhorn: Miss Spark. The catapult: Mister Thunderclap. The cups: also Mister Thunderclap.
    Mother Whitlock: Nothing leaves that cabinet. Except, once in a very long while, for a victor.
    <<flag a2_pr_cab>>
    <<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
-> Ask about Fernanda <<if not flagged("a2_pr_fern")>>
    <<if flagged("won_tess")>>
        Mother Whitlock: The flamingo is home. I heard the squeal from my bath. Well done, I suppose.
    <<else>>
        Mother Whitlock: That flamingo is a lawn ornament with delusions of grandeur. But she is OUR lawn ornament. Do bring her home.
    <<endif>>
    <<flag a2_pr_fern>>
    <<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
-> Ask about Tess <<if flagged("a2_pr_won") and not flagged("a2_pr_tess")>>
    Mother Whitlock: Miss Calloway is the finest president this house has had. She alphabetises her alphabet soup. I could not be prouder.
    <<flag a2_pr_tess>>
    <<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
-> Ask for a cup of tea <<if flagged("a2_pr_won")>>
    Mother Whitlock: (pours) No sugar, I presume.
    Dex: The company is sweet enough.
    Mother Whitlock: Don't push it, Mister Dooley.
    <<jump A2_Whitlock_Menu>>
-> Take your leave
    Mother Whitlock: Good evening, Mister Dooley. Mind the rug. It's older than you and better behaved.
===

title: A2_Duel_Start
---
Mother Whitlock: Very well. The parlor test. Five courtesies. Shoulders back.
Dex: Is there a time limit?
Mother Whitlock: There is a lifetime limit. Begin.
<<unflag a2_pr_slip>>
<<flag a2_pr_tried>>
<<jump A2_Duel1>>
===
title: A2_Duel1
---
Mother Whitlock: What a brave shirt. I could never be so courageous as to dress like a fruit salad.
-> "Thank you. A friend with far better taste than mine helped me choose it." <<if flagged("a2_cb1")>>
    Mother Whitlock: (a tiny nod) Credit given elsewhere. Gracious. One.
    <<jump A2_Duel2>>
-> "At least my fruit salad isn't wearing pearls to bed."
    Mother Whitlock: Rude, and inaccurate. I sleep in a cardigan. That is a slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel2>>
-> "It's not a shirt. It's a lifestyle."
    Mother Whitlock: Then it is a lifestyle with a missing button. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel2>>
===
title: A2_Duel2
---
Mother Whitlock: I expect you're very proud of your little dormitory. Do they let you have a spoon?
-> "We have three spoons. One of them is a fork."
    Mother Whitlock: Then it is a fork. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel3>>
-> "Room 214 has a mini-fridge. Your move."
    Mother Whitlock: A mini-fridge is not a move, Mister Dooley. It is a cry for help. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel3>>
-> "Then I'm all the luckier to be a guest in a house as lovely as this one." <<if flagged("a2_cb2")>>
    Mother Whitlock: (the faintest blush) Flattery of the house. The house accepts. Two.
    <<jump A2_Duel3>>
===
title: A2_Duel3
---
Mother Whitlock: Sugar? One lump or two? Or do they not have sugar where you were raised?
-> "Seven lumps. I'm celebrating."
    Mother Whitlock: Seven lumps is not a celebration. It is a dental emergency. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel4>>
-> "None for me, thank you. The company is sweet enough." <<if flagged("a2_cb3")>>
    Mother Whitlock: ...Oh, that old line. It still works. Drat. Three.
    <<jump A2_Duel4>>
-> "Just pour it straight in my mouth."
    Mother Whitlock: Miss Spark said that too. Look where she is now. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel4>>
===
title: A2_Duel4
---
Mother Whitlock: I would shake your hand, but I've only just had my gloves cleaned.
-> "I washed my hands. Twice. Once with soap."
    Mother Whitlock: Once with soap. And the other time? No, don't tell me. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel5>>
-> "I'll just high-five the air near you."
    Mother Whitlock: The air near me has done nothing to deserve that. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel5>>
-> "Then allow me to bow instead. It's kinder to your gloves and better for my posture." <<if flagged("a2_cb4")>>
    Mother Whitlock: (watches the bow) A bow. How rare. How correct. Four.
    <<jump A2_Duel5>>
===
title: A2_Duel5
---
Mother Whitlock: You have been in my parlor for a full minute, and you haven't said one word about the curtains.
-> "Forgive me, I was speechless. Are they original to the house?" <<if flagged("a2_cb5")>>
    Mother Whitlock: 1921. Hand-dyed. (sniffs) Five.
    <<jump A2_Duel_End>>
-> "They're very... curtain-y."
    Mother Whitlock: They are. That was never in doubt. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel_End>>
-> "I was thinking of borrowing one for a toga."
    Mother Whitlock: Over my cardigan. Slip.
    <<flag a2_pr_slip>>
    <<jump A2_Duel_End>>
===
title: A2_Duel_End
---
<<if flagged("a2_pr_slip")>>
    Mother Whitlock: That will do. It will not do well, but it will do. You have failed, Mister Dooley.
    Mother Whitlock: Do come back when you have better answers. Everyone on this street has lost to me at least once. A few of them learned something.
    Dex: Everyone on Greek Row has lost to her. So everyone on Greek Row knows at least one right answer.
<<else>>
    Mother Whitlock: (sets down her teacup with a click) Five for five. Not since Duncan Pellingham in 2019.
    Mother Whitlock: You are a gentleman, Mister Dooley. Under all that bedsheet. You may reclaim one item from my cabinet.
    <<flag a2_pr_won>>
    <<jump A2_Duel_Reclaim>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Duel_Reclaim
---
Mother Whitlock: Choose carefully. One item.
-> The Disco Volcano record
    Mother Whitlock: (unlocks the cabinet) Miss Spark's record. Tell her the teacups have forgiven her. I have not.
    <<give disco_record>>
    <<flag a2_got_record>>
    Dex: Dolly is going to lose her mind.
-> The airhorn
    Mother Whitlock: Absolutely not. That airhorn is evidence. Choose again.
    <<jump A2_Duel_Reclaim>>
-> The water-balloon catapult
    Mother Whitlock: That is not an item, Mister Dooley. That is a war crime with a bucket. Choose again.
    <<jump A2_Duel_Reclaim>>
===
title: A2_Whitlock_GiveTie
---
Mother Whitlock: You are already wearing one. One is sufficient. Two is a cry for help.
===
title: A2_Whitlock_GiveRecord
---
Mother Whitlock: It has been reclaimed. Take it to Miss Spark before I reconsider. I am reconsidering now.
===
title: A2_Whitlock_GiveFernanda
---
Mother Whitlock: Put that bird on her stand, Mister Dooley. Not on my rug.
===
title: A2_Whitlock_GiveSmoothie
---
Mother Whitlock: That is orange, and it has a straw. I do not consume things with straws.
Dex: So she's not the hungry one. Moose is.
===
title: A2_Whitlock_GiveBeanie
---
Mother Whitlock: Absolutely not. That object has been inside a frat house.
===
title: A2_Whitlock_GiveToken
---
Mother Whitlock: A keepsake. How sentimental. Keep it, Mister Dooley. Keepsakes are for keeping.
===

title: A2_Bar_Enter
---
<<if not flagged("bar_intro")>>
    Dex: The Fuse Box. Candles on every table, a DJ booth, a giant amp, and a silence you could cut with a knife.
    Dolly Spark: Don't say it. I know it's quiet.
    <<flag bar_intro>>
<<elseif flagged("dolly_fused") and not flagged("bar_loud")>>
    Dex: The Fuse Box, alive and pounding. The candles are vibrating.
    <<flag bar_loud>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_BarExit_Look
---
Dex: The door back out to Greek Row.
===
title: A2_BarExit_Use
---
<<go greek_row from_bar>>
===
title: A2_Counter_Look
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused") and not flagged("a2_got_smoothie")>>
    Dex: The blender is back on and making something orange. A sign says "VOLCANO SMOOTHIE: FREE FOR WHOEVER FIXED THE FUSE".
<<else>>
    Dex: A sticky wooden bar lit by candles. A tip jar says "TIPS FOR FUSES".
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Counter_Use
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused") and not flagged("a2_got_smoothie")>>
    Dolly Spark: Blender's back, friend! Grab a Volcano Smoothie. On the house. You earned it.
    Dex: Mango, chilli, and something the bartender calls "courage". It's very orange.
    <<give volcano_smoothie>>
    <<flag a2_got_smoothie>>
<<elseif flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dex: The blender works again. Somebody orders a smoothie and cries a little.
<<else>>
    Dex: The blender's dead, the soda gun's dead, the lights are dead. Even the candles look tired.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_FusePanel_Look
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dex: The fuse panel, with a borrowed frat fuse glowing happily in the socket.
<<else>>
    Dex: The bar's fuse panel. One socket, one blackened, extremely dead fuse. "30A" is scratched on the door.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_FusePanel_Use
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dex: It's working. I'm not touching it.
<<else>>
    Dex: I unscrew the dead fuse. It's toasted. I screw it back in out of politeness.
    Dex: I need an old thirty-amp screw-in fuse. Nobody's made those in decades.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Board_Look
---
Dex: A chalkboard: "DJ DOLLY SPARK TONIGHT! Requests welcome." Underneath, smaller: "Dolly's number one favourite song: DISCO VOLCANO."
<<flag know_dolly_song>>
===
title: A2_Board_Use
---
Dex: Somebody wrote "TOGA TOGA TOGA" underneath. Somebody else crossed it out very hard.
<<flag know_dolly_song>>
===
title: A2_Booth_Look
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dex: Two turntables spinning and a laptop covered in stickers. Pure power.
<<else>>
    Dex: Two turntables, a laptop covered in stickers, and zero electricity.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Booth_Use
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dolly Spark: Hands off the decks, friend. You can request, not touch.
<<else>>
    Dex: Turntables with no power. Like a car with no wheels. Or a duck with no quack.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Amp_Look
---
Dex: An amp the size of a fridge. Somebody painted "BIG BERTHA" on the side. This is what keeps eating the fuse.
===
title: A2_Amp_Use
---
Dolly Spark: Don't touch Bertha. She's sensitive. She just blows fuses when she's happy.
===

title: A2_Dolly_Look
---
<<if flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dex: Dolly Spark, glowing neon in the dark and bouncing to Disco Volcano. Again.
<<else>>
    Dex: Neon hair, headphones, and a denim jacket held together by more safety pins than jacket.
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Dolly_Talk
---
<<if flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: (over the music) FRIEND! You saved my night!
<<elseif has("disco_record")>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_GiveRecord>>
<<elseif flagged("a2_know_record")>>
    Dolly Spark: Power, yes. Bertha, happy. Disco Volcano, still locked in Mother Whitlock's cabinet. So close, friend.
<<elseif flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dolly Spark: Power's back! Okay, friend, the first request is yours.
<<elseif not flagged("met_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: Hey. Welcome to the quietest bar on Greek Row. I'm Dolly Spark. I'm the DJ. Allegedly.
    Dex: Dex. Where's the music?
    Dolly Spark: (points at the amp) Big Bertha blew the fuse. Third time tonight. And that was the bar's last spare.
    Dolly Spark: It's the ancient screw-in kind. Thirty amps. They stopped making them before I was born.
    Dolly Spark: Only the oldest houses on this street still have them. Find me one and I'll play you anything.
    <<flag met_dolly>>
<<else>>
    Dolly Spark: No fuse, no music. I'm just a girl standing in the dark with a lot of safety pins.
<<endif>>
<<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Dolly_Menu
---
-> Make the first request <<if flagged("dolly_fused") and not flagged("a2_know_record") and not flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: What do you want to hear, friend?
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Request>>
-> Ask for a safety pin <<if not flagged("got_pin")>>
    <<if flagged("met_chad")>>
        Dex: I need to make a toga. Could I borrow a safety pin?
        Dolly Spark: A toga for the frat? Ha. Every DJ carries emergency pins. Wardrobe malfunctions, broken headphones, broken hearts.
        Dolly Spark: Here. Pin responsibly.
        <<give safety_pin>>
        <<flag got_pin>>
    <<else>>
        Dolly Spark: What for?
        Dex: ...I don't know yet.
        Dolly Spark: Come back when you've got a reason. These pins are load-bearing.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Ask where to find a fuse <<if not flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dolly Spark: Old thirty-amp screw-in. Try the oldest house on the street. Hint: it's the loud one.
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Ask about her favourite song <<if not flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: "Disco Volcano." Six minutes of bass that hits you like lava. It's on the board. It's always on the board.
    <<flag know_dolly_song>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Ask about the confiscated record <<if flagged("a2_know_record") and not flagged("won_dolly") and not flagged("a2_dolly_rec")>>
    Dolly Spark: Okay, confession. I was a Phi Lambda Alpha sister. For one semester.
    Dolly Spark: At the Founders' Tea, I played Disco Volcano. With the airhorn. The teacups started dancing. A great-aunt fainted.
    Dolly Spark: Mother Whitlock confiscated the record "until a gentleman reclaims it". Nobody's reclaimed anything from her since 2019.
    Dolly Spark: She lives in the sorority parlor. Gentlemen need a necktie just to get through the door.
    <<flag a2_dolly_rec>>
    <<flag a2_know_tie_rule>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Ask how she lost to Mother Whitlock <<if (flagged("a2_dolly_rec") or flagged("a2_pr_tried")) and not flagged("a2_cb3")>>
    Dolly Spark: She did the sugar thing. "One lump or two, or do they not have sugar where you were raised?"
    Dolly Spark: I said "Just pour it straight in my mouth." Big mistake. Tess told me the right answer afterwards. AFTERWARDS.
    Dolly Spark: It's "None for me, thank you. The company is sweet enough." Gross, right? It works on her every time.
    <<flag a2_cb3>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Ask about the bracelet <<if flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: It means you're with the DJ. Flash it at any party and they'll let you near the speakers.
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Ask for another song <<if flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: Disco Volcano again? Excellent choice. I'll put it on loop. I had it on loop anyway.
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> Say goodbye
    <<if flagged("won_dolly")>>
        Dolly Spark: Bye, friend! Don't blow any fuses on your way out.
    <<else>>
        Dolly Spark: Cool. I'll be here. In the dark. Or the light. Depends on you, honestly.
    <<endif>>
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveFuse
---
<<if flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dolly Spark: One fuse is plenty, friend. Bertha and I have promised to behave.
<<else>>
    Dolly Spark: Is that... a thirty-amp screw-in fuse? Where did you even... No. Don't tell me.
    Dolly Spark: (screws it into the panel) Lights! Power! Bertha, say hello!
    Dex: The amp hums like a happy hippo. The candles look relieved.
    <<take frat_fuse>>
    <<flag dolly_fused>>
    <<flag met_dolly>>
    <<flag bar_loud>>
    Dolly Spark: You absolute legend. The first request is yours. What do you want to hear?
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Request>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Dolly_Request
---
-> "Disco Volcano"
    Dolly Spark: (gasps) You know Disco Volcano? Nobody requests Disco Volcano. Except me. Constantly.
    Dolly Spark: (digs through her record crate) ...It's not here. Oh no. It's not here because SHE has it.
    Dolly Spark: Mother Whitlock. The sorority housemother. She confiscated it. Long story. Ask me about it.
    <<flag a2_know_record>>
    <<flag know_dolly_song>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
-> "Hank Hollister Live"
    Dolly Spark: Country? In MY booth? Respect, but no. Think harder, friend. What's my jam?
    <<if not flagged("know_dolly_song")>>
        Dex: Her favourite song. Maybe it's written somewhere in here.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Request>>
-> "Toga Toga Toga"
    Dolly Spark: Absolutely not. That song is banned in three states and this bar.
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Request>>
-> Let me think about it
    Dolly Spark: Take your time. First requests are sacred.
    <<jump A2_Dolly_Menu>>
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveRecord
---
<<if flagged("won_dolly")>>
    Dolly Spark: Already spinning, friend!
<<elseif not flagged("dolly_fused")>>
    Dolly Spark: My record! Which I can't play, because there's no power. Hang on to it till Bertha's breathing again.
<<else>>
    Dolly Spark: My RECORD! You got it out of Mother Whitlock's cabinet? Nobody gets anything out of that cabinet!
    Dex: I complimented her curtains.
    Dolly Spark: You absolute diplomat. (drops the needle)
    Dex: The bass hits. The floor shakes. Dolly dances like nobody's watching. I'm watching. It's great.
    Dolly Spark: Okay, you're officially my favourite person tonight. Here, a glow-stick bracelet. It means you're with the DJ.
    <<take disco_record>>
    <<give glow_bracelet>>
    <<flag won_dolly>>
    <<flag know_dolly_song>>
<<endif>>
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveSheet
---
Dolly Spark: Cute, but I'm not dressing up as a ghost tonight. Maybe next Halloween.
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveFernanda
---
Dolly Spark: Is that the sorority flamingo? You should get her home before Tess Calloway sends a search party. With clipboards.
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveTie
---
Dolly Spark: A clip-on? I'm a DJ, friend, not a substitute teacher. Wear it to the parlor.
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveSmoothie
---
Dolly Spark: That's for you, friend. Or for someone hungrier. I run on bass.
===
title: A2_Dolly_GiveBeanie
---
Dolly Spark: A frat pledge beanie? I'd rather wear Bertha.
===

title: Item_bedsheet_Look
---
Dex: A plain white bedsheet, borrowed from the sorority. It smells like lavender and organisation.
===
title: Item_safety_pin_Look
---
Dex: A big safety pin from Dolly's jacket. Pin responsibly.
===
title: Item_toga_Look
---
Dex: My homemade toga. A bedsheet with ambition, pinned at the shoulder.
===
title: Item_frat_fuse_Look
---
Dex: An old screw-in fuse, stamped "30A". It used to keep a whole frat house lit.
===
title: Item_fernanda_Look
---
Dex: Fernanda, seven feet of inflatable flamingo, folded awkwardly under my arm. She looks judgemental.
===
title: Item_sorority_pin_Look
---
Dex: Tess Calloway's sorority pin, pink and gold with the house letters on it. I'm a friend of the house.
===
title: Item_glow_bracelet_Look
---
Dex: Dolly's glow-stick bracelet. It means I'm with the DJ. It also means my wrist is green.
===
title: Item_volcano_smoothie_Look
---
Dex: A Volcano Smoothie. Mango, chilli and "courage". It's so orange it's almost loud. I'm not hungry, but somebody is.
===
title: Item_clip_on_tie_Look
---
Dex: Moose's clip-on necktie. Navy blue, with a tiny moose on it. Proof that I am a gentleman caller.
===
title: Item_pledge_beanie_Look
---
Dex: A blue pledge beanie that says PLEDGE across the front. In the dark, this is my whole identity.
===
title: Item_disco_record_Look
---
Dex: "Disco Volcano", on vinyl. Six minutes of bass. The sleeve still smells faintly of tea.
===
